  "worked_solution": "We model the value of the art object using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nV(t)={V}_{0}\\,{e}^{kt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${V}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that  it was initially worth $$2\\,000,$ so we have ${V}_{0}=2\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the value $V$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nV(t)=2\\,000\\,{e}^{kt}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $k,$ we substitute $V(10)=10\\,000$ into the equation above and solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(10) & =2\\,000\\,{e}^{k\\cdot 10} \\\\ 10\\,000 & =2\\,000\\,{e}^{10k} \\\\ {e}^{10k} & =\\frac{10\\,000}{2\\,000} \\\\ {e}^{10k} & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}\u2061({e}^{10k}) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(5) \\\\ 10k & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(5) \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(5) \\\\ k & \u22480.16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k\u224816%,$ rounded to the nearest percent.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
